      "countAsQuest:1": 1,
      "desc:8": "Old missile bases lie buried in the Overworld and on every planet with solid ground. A complex is about 240 by 240 blocks and 24 blocks down: a hub, wide halls, 35 to 40 rooms and a gallery of four to ten real silos. On the surface you see only concrete shafts, sometimes a small radar hut, and an escape-ladder trapdoor.\n\nNothing in a complex is better than its planet\u0027s ceiling: EV in the Overworld and on the Moon, one voltage tier more for each rocket tier above. Bring back proof: a block of Silo Complex Wall, or a damaged missile body from a salvage chest. The damaged body can\u0027t be placed or flown, but it recycles for its plates.\n\n[warn]Operational complexes have guards at their posts, and a post you break stays broken.[/warn]",
